<title>FRANCE: FRANCE REVISES UP SUGAR BEET AREA.</title>
<headline>FRANCE REVISES UP SUGAR BEET AREA.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The French farm ministry on Tuesday revised up its estimate for France's sugar beet plantings this year to 467,000 hectares from 455,000 hectares.</p>
<p>The revised figure, published by statistics office SCEES, is 10,000 hectares above last year's crop area of 457,000 hectares.</p>
<p>The ministry has yet to publish 1997 yield or production estimates for sugar beet.</p>
</text>
